I got this old php/js project with bootstrap. I heavily use xslt styles to generate sql, php and js files.
I use my own php and javascript libraries.
The idea is like this: I have a build/medatata.xml file with all project objects. If I need a new
model/controller/enum etc I modify the metadata.xml file, then run a build process that
uses xslt styles to construct sql migrations, model, controller php and js files.
I use templates to modify code:
build/templates/controller/*_Controller_php.xsl
build/templates/controller/*_Controller_js.xsl
models practically never changes, but still there are templates:
build/templates/models/*_Model_php.xsl
build/templates/models/*_Model_js.xsl
So real files live in controls and models, or for javascript files in js20/controls and js20/models.
I never edit models/controllers files, just templates.
I have a huge js library in js20/core and js20/controls.
What javascript files are included in the project is also defind by the metadata.xml file.

common.zip and osbe.zip are in php include directory. Common directory stores some common functions/libraries used
in a project. OSBE folder contains php classes used for building the project.

